# Memrize (OmniRoute)

OmniRoute uses **Memrize** for persistent memory. Battle-test it on real work in this repo.

## Databases

| Layer | Path | Use |
|-------|------|-----|
| Project | `.memrize/memrize.db` | Architecture, decisions, bugs, session learnings for OmniRoute |
| Global | `~/.memrize/global.db` | User rules + cross-project facts (Andrew prefs, infra) |

**Never** rely on `./memrize.db` in repo root — that is an empty CLI default trap. Always use `--db` or MCP.

## Session start

1. Call **`memrize_get_context`** on `memrize-omniroute` (project) and/or `memrize-global` (user rules).
2. Or run: `scripts/memrize/context.sh`

## During work

- **`memrize_remember`** — significant decisions, root-cause findings, API quirks discovered
- **`memrize_search`** — before re-investigating something already solved
- **`memrize_pin_rule`** — only for project-specific invariants (global rules live in global DB)
- **`memrize_record_failure`** / `scripts/memrize/report-error.sh` — bugs, test failures, MCP issues

## Dogfooding feedback

When Memrize itself misbehaves (wrong DB, corrupt forget, MCP errors), record it:

```bash
scripts/memrize/report-error.sh test_failure "short title" '{"component":"..."}'
```

This feeds Achiles `NEXT_DEV_PROJECT=memrize` for fixes.

## Env

Source once per terminal: `source scripts/memrize/env.sh`

Setup / rebuild: `scripts/memrize/setup.sh`
